# Sandbox

Containerised dev environment so coding agents can't reach the host filesystem
or your shell's secrets. The repo is mounted at `/workspace`; everything else is
ephemeral.

## Quick start

```bash
just sandbox-build      # build the image (once)
just sandbox-init       # generate missing secrets into .env (idempotent)
just sandbox-enable-user-instructions  # optional: selected global rules, read-only
just sandbox-up         # start supporting services
just sandbox-shell      # drop into the sandbox shell
just sandbox-down       # tear down
```

Prefer `op://…` 1Password references in `.env` and start with
`op run --env-file=.env -- just sandbox-up`. The `agent-home` Docker volume
persists CLI logins; `just sandbox-nuke` deletes that credential-bearing volume.
Global Claude/Codex instructions remain isolated unless you explicitly run
`just sandbox-enable-user-instructions`; the generated local override is
git-ignored and never mounts complete agent config directories.

